WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.206
- Oh, my gosh. I'm so excited to meet you!

00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:04.039
- [Cristo] Oh, thank you very much.

00:00:04.039 --> 00:00:05.340
- I love the show!

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.740
I know I said that in the card I gave you,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.250
but I'm still obsessed with the show.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.300
I scream "football is life," all the time.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.290
Meet JoJo though. Y'all get to meet now.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.123
- Nice to meet you.

00:00:13.123 --> 00:00:14.100
- Nice to meet you.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.070
- So you really are a
football player, right?

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.380
- Yeah. Well, I mean, I
used to play professionally,

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.780
since I was a kid.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.613
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:00:21.613 --> 00:00:25.170
- Yeah, my grandma,
when I started to walk,

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.180
my grandma taught me how to
play in the garage of my house.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.550
I was always carrying a ball with me.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.570
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.610
- Yeah, football was
part of me since a kid,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.010
then playing professionally when I was 15.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.430
And then later in life, I
stopped when I decided to study.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.740
And my parents told me to
study and intelligently,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:46.690
because I had some injuries,

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.340
but then yeah, football
has been part of my life.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.811
- Oh, my God. It's so fitting.

00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:53.470
So this is actually my
favorite thing about you,

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.520
that I learned, I didn't know,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.470
you know like so many languages.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:57.303
- Yes.

00:00:57.303 --> 00:00:59.310
- I think that's amazing! What
all languages do you know?

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.163
- I speak English of course, I think.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.770
French, German, and a bit of Italian,

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.160
and Spanish is my mother tongue.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:08.993
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.620
Okay, could you teach us

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:14.130
how to say "football is life" in French?

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.076
- In French.

00:01:15.076 --> 00:01:16.659
(speaking French)

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:17.492
- In German.

00:01:17.492 --> 00:01:18.883
(speaking German)

00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:19.833
(Kelly speaking in German)

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:21.320
(Cristo repeating German phrase)

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.074
- Foosball, that's like the other movies.

00:01:23.074 --> 00:01:24.960
(JoJo speaking in German)

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.410
- So how did you land
the role on "Ted Lasso,"

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.580
other than being perfect for it?

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:30.480
- Well, thank you.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.430
Well, I started my master
in acting in the UK.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.700
I saved money over there
and before going to the UK,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.870
and then I was in Mexico

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.000
and I received the
audition for "Ted Lasso."

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.610
I did it, didn't hear anything.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:45.740
They started shooting in August.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.040
So I thought, well, nothing happened.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.630
But then I received a random
tweet from Bill Lawrence,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:51.790
a showrunner of the show,

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:54.287
who said just, "good audition, man."

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.330
And I was like, okay,

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.660
either he's playing with my feelings

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.650
or there's something good happening.

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.425
- Oh, my God. That'd be so mean.

00:02:02.425 --> 00:02:05.980
- Yeah. And then I did more auditions,

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.840
and story short, I got the
role for an Icelandic man.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.100
So when I arrived on
set I was called Gooner,

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.490
and I was like, if I'm
playing an Icelandic man,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.580
I need more preparation.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.210
- Wait, what?

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.540
So originally it wasn't even
the role you're in right now?

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.480
- No, no, no.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.530
The role was for a guy from Iceland,

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.160
but they liked my audition,
from what I know now,

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.950
that they kept it

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:33.376
and that's why they
adapted it to who I am.

00:02:33.376 --> 00:02:36.238
- Oh, my God. I love
it! You were so great!

00:02:36.238 --> 00:02:37.843
That's amazing.

00:02:37.843 --> 00:02:40.590
But are you getting recognized everywhere?

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.840
- Well, yeah, here in LA.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.400
This is where I realized that the bit of

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.683
the craziness around the show,
which I'm grateful and stuff.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.240
Yeah. Lots of fans.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.150
I have a funny anecdote
that recently, well,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.313
I was in a commercial
center, I went to the toilet,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.020
and then I was about to wee

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.800
and I just feel someone staring at me.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.440
And I'm like...

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.120
And then this guy, very happy,

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.070
and he just says, "are you the
smiley guy from "Ted Lasso?"

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.590
Not even my character,
and I'm like, "yeah."

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.587
And he's goes like,
"can I have a picture?"

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.400
- Can you give me a minute?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.233
- Not right now.

00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:24.160
- And I was like, "um, okay."

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.370
- You're like, shaking! Ha ha.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.960
- And then we got this selfie,

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.080
and he just, "thank you,
man," and he leaves.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.380
And I was like, "what
the hell just happened?"

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.430
- That has happened to me in a bathroom.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.950
I have literally, I went in the bathroom,

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.680
I sat down to pee and literally,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.320
someone just slid paper
and pen under the thing.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.477
And I was like, "all right."

00:03:45.052 --> 00:03:46.477
- If you've got the guts to do that!

00:03:46.477 --> 00:03:49.477
I was like, if you're okay with it.

00:03:50.343 --> 00:03:53.410
This is your opportunity.
I get it, seize the moment.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.750
Has that ever happened
to you? Anything weird?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.330
- Oh, yeah. bathrooms are just,

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.200
- [Kelly] You get trapped.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.150
- You get trapped.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.860
And it's the worst one like for me,

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.220
'cause it's like, teenage
girls just follow me in

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.710
and it'll be like a squad.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.610
You know, if I go to Disneyland

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.970
there's like, squads of
teenage girls that'll go,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.360
and they'll follow me into a bathroom.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.030
And then you come out and you're bombarded

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:15.510
with seven random girls
just waiting there.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.600
And you're like, "hello, thank you."

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.757
- Yeah. I hope, I please
hope that you just go,

00:04:19.757 --> 00:04:22.407
"it all went well, thank
you," and just keep walking.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.820
The show is nominated for a lot of Emmys

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.219
and you were also nominated
for an Imagen, right?

00:04:29.219 --> 00:04:31.801
- Yeah. Oh, thank you guys. Yeah.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.500
I'm very happy for the nominations

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.640
for the show in the Emmys.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.733
But yeah, we got this Imagen award,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.160
which awards, Latin talent.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.500
And I'm just very grateful.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.900
and especially with the
people I'm nominated with.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.950
And I share the news with my family

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.920
and my family was more excited

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.138
with the fact that I was
nominated with Mario Lopez.

00:04:55.138 --> 00:04:56.660
(laughing)

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:58.100
Because, I grew up...

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.810
Yeah. Yeah. I love that.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:00.643
- [Kelly] I love Mario.

00:05:00.643 --> 00:05:02.270
I love him, and we love him.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.919
And I grew up watching
"Saved by the Bell,"

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:05.752
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:05:05.752 --> 00:05:07.510
so my parents were like,
"oh, my God. I love this!"

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.420
- I want to be in "Zack
Attack." Yeah, that's cool.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.230
I want to be in "Zack
Attack," very much so.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.063
He was always cool.

00:05:12.063 --> 00:05:13.753
He made the Speedo look very nice.

